// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Two call sites to the same procedure share ONE activation context
// (--graph-snapshot shows both "enter square(...)" edges landing on the
// same cluster_ctx_1): square's summary is the join over every call site,
// not resolved per call site. So each combine reads back join([9,9],
// [16,16]) = [9,16], not its own call's exact argument -- a is really 9 and
// b is really 16, but both checks see the same widened [9,16] range. This
// is call-site (in)sensitivity, the same flow-insensitive-summary
// discipline the D/G global path uses (see 04-globals/known-imprecision/
// 01-global_var.vimp), applied here to procedure activations instead of
// globals.
void square(n) {
  return n * n
}
void main() {
  a := square(3);
  b := square(4);
  __voblint_check(a == 9); // UNKNOWN
  __voblint_check(b == 16) // UNKNOWN
}
